# Environment files hold connection strings, keys and per-deployment choices. `.env.example` is the
# tracked TEMPLATE; every real `.env.<environment>` stays out of git — `.env.local`, `.env.dev`,
# `.env.test`, `.env.live` and (while the port lasts) `.env.postgres` / `.env.sqlserver` /
# `.env.swpostgres`. The project copier (`altea-upgrade clone`) copies them into a new application
# anyway; they simply are not part of its first commit, so sharing one is a deliberate force-add.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Synchronization scripts written by `terminal sync` — a throwaway artefact of one
# database's drift, reviewed then applied. A migration you KEEP goes to eastwind/Migrations.
terminal/sync/
